READING: with the round-2 FUNCTION wrapper the driver rc IS the return value on bash 3.2 AND bash 5.2 (return 1 -> 1, 0 -> 0, 7 -> 7 at ERRORS=2), so a `return 0` tamper would make E1 (rc != 0) RED; the round-1 top-level driver (CONTROL) gives 1 (bash 3.2) / 2 (bash 5.2) for every N. The UNCONDITIONAL tamper gives rc 1 at ERRORS=0, so E2 would RED. The round-2 mktemp template succeeds under GNU coreutils 9.7 where the round-1 form is refused (CONTROL). This is the block driven the way the test drives it, NOT the test suite: the gate runs the suite.
Side effect: the macOS CONTROL `mktemp -t` created one empty file under the user TMPDIR (/var/folders/.../T/ks1054_summary_drive.*); nothing else outside <g46_sp>.
